/** \file p4.dox
 * \brief User's Guide for Pixel Prediction Post-Processing and p4Reduce.
 * \author Jared R. Males
 */

/** \addtogroup p4reduce_user_guide
 * @{
 *
 * P4 (Pixel Prediction Post-Processing) predicts the time-variable stellar PSF and noise at one search pixel from a
 * local annular-wedge optimization region (OR). By default the complete time sequence trains one in-sample regression
 * for each search pixel. KLIP-compatible ADI exclusion can instead refit the model separately for every target frame.
 * A central exclusion disk prevents the expected companion location from entering the predictor set.
 * This guide describes the detector-frame algorithm, which is the P4 science path and the only regression frame that
 * should be used for reductions. The separate
 * \ref p4_rotated_user_guide "rotated-frame negative-result page" documents an unsuccessful experiment for historical
 * and numerical-reference purposes.
 *
 * \section p4reduce_detector_regression Detector-frame regression
 *
 * For one fixed detector search pixel indexed by \f$n\f$, let \f$\mathbf{y}_n\f$ be its `T x 1` time series and let `X` contain `K` interpolated
 * predictor-pixel time series. P4 eigendecomposes the smaller of the two
 * <a href=https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gram_matrix>Gram</a> matrices.
 * For `T <= K` it forms the temporal Gram matrix
 *
 * \f[
 *     G_T = X X^T
 * \f]
 *
 * and subtracts each retained temporal eigenvector `u` as `u (u^T y)`. For `T > K` it forms the predictor Gram
 * matrix
 *
 * \f[
 *   G_K = X^T X
 * \f]
 *
 * and `b = X^T y`, then applies the algebraically equivalent truncated pseudoinverse. Both
 * branches solve an `N x N` symmetric problem with `N = min(T,K)`, use the same nonzero eigenvalues and rank policy,
 * and add no hidden centering or intercept. Mean-image subtraction and other preprocessing are controlled entirely
 * by the inherited hciReduce preprocessing configuration.
 *
 * With the compatibility default `p4.numberImages=0`, each predictor row contains only the `K` OR pixels from its
 * central image. A positive `p4.numberImages=N` appends `N` nearest qualifying earlier-image blocks and `N` nearest
 * qualifying later-image blocks. The central block retains its `K_OR` OR pixels, while each neighbor contributes
 * only the `K_PSF` direct detector pixels inside `p4.psfRadius`, for `K_OR + 2N K_PSF` columns. At a cube endpoint,
 * missing neighbors on one temporal side are replaced by additional qualifying images from the available side,
 * preserving both predictor width and integration time. A neighbor qualifies when its wrapped field-rotation
 * displacement is at least `2 * p4.psfRadius` at that annulus's mean search radius, keeping the neighbor's physical
 * PSF disk free of companion signal. If the requested radius cannot retain a structurally valid PCA sample set, P4
 * uses the largest positive radius that does; if no positive radius works, that annulus gracefully reverts to
 * same-image predictors.
 *
 * The detector-frame residual cubes are derotated by the shared ADI final-processing stage before combination.
 *
 * \section p4reduce_modes Application modes
 *
 * `p4Reduce` supports `basic` and `normal` as exact aliases. Each performs one configured target-only ADI reduction.
 * Grid scheduling is deliberately external to the executable. Saved-product `postprocess` mode is not yet supported:
 * it requires a versioned raw-residual and validity-mask checkpoint format so invalid pixels cannot contaminate a
 * resumed derotation or combination.
 *
 * \section p4reduce_configuration P4 configuration
 *
 * The application reuses the ordinary hciReduce input, mask, fake-injection, preprocessing, coaddition, ADI,
 * combination, and output settings. P4 adds only these targets:
 *
 * | Target | Contract |
 * |---|---|
 * | `geom.minRadius`, `geom.maxRadius` | Matching, ordered, non-overlapping full-annulus bounds. Inner radii are inclusive and outer radii are exclusive. |
 * | `adi.excludeMethod` | `none` preserves the in-sample fit. `pixel`, `angle`, and `imno` select references for target-frame exclusion within the inclusive `adi.minDPx` threshold, with the same semantics as KLIP. |
 * | `adi.minDPx` | Nonnegative exclusion threshold: pixels at the annulus inner radius for `pixel`, degrees for `angle`, or target-row distance for `imno`. A non-`none` method with zero excludes exactly the target row. |
 * | `p4.exclusionSolver` | Held-out regression solver: `explicitRefit` (default) or the opt-in `factorDowndateExact` correctness backend. This target requires a non-`none` `adi.excludeMethod`. |
 * | `p4.numberImages` | Nonnegative count of qualifying earlier and later detector frames added to each predictor row; `0` is the compatibility default. |
 * | `p4.modeFractions` | Finite, strictly increasing fractions in `(0,1]`. Each annulus realizes `floor(fraction * min(T,K))`; zero or duplicate realized counts are rejected. |
 * | `p4.orDeltaRadiusInner`, `p4.orDeltaRadiusOuter` | Positive inward and outward radial extents of the local predictor wedge, in pixels. |
 * | `p4.orArcHalfWidth` | Nonnegative azimuthal half-width expressed as arc length in pixels; `0` uses only `p4.orMaxHalfAngle`. |
 * | `p4.orMaxHalfAngle` | Angular half-width cap in `(0,180]` degrees; `180` permits the full 360-degree annulus. |
 * | `p4.psfRadius` | Positive physical radius of the central signal-exclusion disk, in pixels. |
 * | `p4.exclusionPolicy` | Required `sampleCenter` or `kernelSupport` policy. |
 * | `p4.exclusionRadiusBuffer` | Explicit nonnegative amount added to `p4.psfRadius`; `0.5` reproduces the prototype's effective mask buffer. |
 * | `p4.rankTolerance` | Relative eigenvalue threshold in `[0,1)`, default `1e-12`. |
 * | `p4.memoryFraction` | Fraction of Linux `MemAvailable` reserved for future P4 allocations, default `0.8`; `0` disables automatic worker limiting. |
 * | `p4.writeDiagnostics` | Enable ownership, validity, canonical-region, rank, and timing FITS diagnostics. Every diagnostic records `HIERARCH P4 FRAME`. |
 * | `p4.diagnosticDirectory` | Optional explicit destination override; `.` groups diagnostics with the run's other auxiliary products. |
 *
 * P4 rejects configured RDI input, overlapping annuli, and nonfinite target input as hard errors. The geometry must
 * fit its configured detector-frame interpolation footprints. Target-frame exclusion requires detector-frame
 * regression, `p4.numberImages=0`, no pixel-local processing, and no frozen-model PSF calculation. Rank support is
 * tracked independently for every target and output mode.
 *
 * \subsection p4reduce_exclusion_solvers Target-frame exclusion solvers
 *
 * `explicitRefit` is the default and numerical oracle. For every target frame, it materializes the retained-row
 * complement and directly refits that target's retained design. `factorDowndateExact` instead factors one immutable,
 * complete safely represented base design for each search pixel, then independently removes each target's deleted
 * rows with mxlib's dense `leadingCovariance` SVD-deletion backend. Downdates are never chained between targets. The
 * science rank threshold is applied after deletion, so it is not used to truncate the base factorization.
 *
 * An unsafe or inconsistent complete base, or a deletion-solver failure, rejects the reduction. One deliberately
 * recorded exception protects the strict post-deletion rank decision: if a downdated eigenvalue is numerically
 * indistinguishable from `p4.rankTolerance * lambdaMax`, P4 recomputes every target fit for that search pixel with
 * the explicit oracle. The number of recomputed target fits is reported and stored in the FITS provenance, so this
 * fallback cannot silently change the backend history. The current dense deletion core still solves a `q x q`
 * symmetric problem for every target. It is a correctness integration and may provide little speedup, or be slower,
 * when `q` approaches the structural rank. A later structured diagonal-minus-low-rank solver is needed before a
 * performance benefit should be assumed.
 *
 * Exclusion selection is stored as deleted rows rather than one retained-row vector per target. `imno` windows use
 * compact half-open spans, including their naturally shortened dataset endpoints without wraparound. `angle` and
 * `pixel` selections use flattened sorted index lists with target offsets. The explicit oracle constructs a retained
 * complement only while evaluating a target. This removes the persistent `O(T^2)` retained-index table while keeping
 * identical selection semantics for both solvers.
 *
 * Science products record the backend and its numerical state in FITS cards. The principal provenance cards are
 * `HIERARCH P4 EXCLUSION SOLVER`, `HIERARCH P4 RANK MODEL`, `HIERARCH P4 FULL BASE`, and
 * `HIERARCH P4 DELETION BACKEND`. Storage and rank diagnostics are recorded by
 * `HIERARCH P4 TARGET EXCLUSION BYTES`, `HIERARCH P4 BASE RANK`, `HIERARCH P4 MAX DELETED ROWS`,
 * `HIERARCH P4 EXCLUSION STORAGE BYTES`, `HIERARCH P4 DELETION CLAMPS`, and
 * `HIERARCH P4 EXPLICIT FALLBACKS`, with per-annulus values where applicable. `HIERARCH P4 MINIMUM RANK` continues
 * to report the minimum post-exclusion numerical rank.
 *
 * `sampleCenter` reproduces the prototype's center-only signal exclusion. `kernelSupport` rejects a predictor when
 * its nominal cubic footprint intersects the exclusion disk.
 *
 * The rank test is the literal strict comparison `lambda > p4.rankTolerance * lambdaMax`. A zero tolerance therefore
 * accepts every eigenvalue returned as positive, including roundoff-positive numerical nulls. Use a nonzero relative
 * tolerance when reliable classification of rank deficiencies matters.
 *
 * \section p4reduce_products Output organization
 *
 * A normal P4 run keeps only the ordinary `finim_NNNN.fits` and, when requested, its
 * `finim_filtered_NNNN.fits` science product directly in `output.directory`. Auxiliary products are grouped under
 * `finim_NNNN_outputs/`. This includes pixel-local validity, per-frame PSF-subtracted products and weights, enabled
 * ownership/rank/timing diagnostics, frozen-model PSF products, optimizer summaries and merit tables, best-fit
 * residual and validity cubes, configuration fragments, and jackknife tables. An exact final filename
 * `<stem>.fits` uses `<stem>_outputs/`.
 *
 * `p4.diagnosticDirectory` retains an explicit override for diagnostics that intentionally belong elsewhere. Leave
 * it at `.` to use the grouped run directory.
 *
 * \section p4reduce_memory Memory-bounded execution
 *
 * When a final combination is requested and `output.outputPSFSub=false`, P4 retains regression residuals only at the
 * owned search pixels. It materializes one full residual cube and one full validity cube at a time, runs the ordinary
 * post-median, derotation, and combination lifecycle for that output mode, retains the combined two-dimensional
 * plane, then releases the temporary cubes before processing the next mode. The final FITS plane order and numerical
 * values are unchanged. `combine.method=none` retains all full residual cubes because they are then the requested
 * result; `output.outputPSFSub=true` also uses the retained-cube path so every per-frame product remains available.
 *
 * P4 estimates private PCA workspace from each annulus's temporal sample count, predictor count, requested output
 * count, selected exclusion solver, and maximum deleted-row count. The estimate includes the exact factor backend's
 * base factors, dense core, rotations, deletion scratch, and mxlib workspace. With the default
 * `p4.memoryFraction=0.8`, Linux `MemAvailable` supplies a future-allocation budget. P4 first verifies that compact
 * residuals, compact deleted-row patterns, and one materialized output pair fit, then caps that annulus's OpenMP
 * worker count so its compact storage plus the estimated concurrent workspaces remain inside the budget. A lower
 * `OMP_NUM_THREADS` value is always respected. The selected and pre-limit worker counts and the per-worker estimate
 * are printed before regression and recorded in the FITS header. If Linux memory discovery is unavailable, P4 emits
 * a warning and retains the OpenMP maximum. Set `p4.memoryFraction=0` to request that behavior explicitly.
 * During geometry construction, `p4Reduce` reports each annulus together with its search-pixel and retained predictor
 * counts. During regression, a rate-limited `std::cerr` status line combines the active annulus's completed/total
 * pixels, measured seconds per pixel, and local ETA with cumulative completed/total pixels
 * across all annuli. Each annulus ends with an exact newline-delimited completion record, so redirected logs remain
 * readable as well as interactive terminal output.
 *
 * \section p4reduce_example Example configuration
 *
 * This compact example follows the public AF Lep/NACO prototype science geometry and adds a `[3.5,6)` calculation
 * annulus for the current inner-boundary support experiment. Paths remain for the user to select. A checked
 * comparison configuration is provided at `examples/p4Reduce_afLepNaco_prototype.conf` and installed under
 * `share/hcireduce/examples`. It uses the prototype's input path, `p4.rankTolerance=0`, and the sequential `finim_`
 * output prefix. With `exactFName=false`, `output.fileName` is a literal prefix rather than a format string, so this
 * produces `finim_0000.fits` and then the next unused four-digit name.
 *
 * \code{.ini}
 * mode=normal
 *
 * [input]
 * directory=/path/to/preprocessed
 * prefix=pp_
 * extension=.fits
 * dateKeyword=
 * angleKeyword=POSANG
 * angleScale=1
 * angleConstant=1.6
 *
 * [geom]
 * minRadius=3.5,6,8,10,12,14,16,18
 * maxRadius=6,8,10,12,14,16,18,20
 *
 * [p4]
 * numberImages=1
 * modeFractions=0.01,0.03,0.05,0.07,0.09,0.11,0.13,0.15,0.17,0.19,0.21,0.23,0.25,0.27,0.29
 * orDeltaRadiusInner=8
 * orDeltaRadiusOuter=30
 * orArcHalfWidth=32
 * orMaxHalfAngle=90
 * psfRadius=1.5
 * exclusionPolicy=sampleCenter
 * exclusionRadiusBuffer=0.5
 * rankTolerance=1e-12
 * memoryFraction=0.8
 * writeDiagnostics=false
 * diagnosticDirectory=.
 *
 * [preProcess]
 * skip=true
 *
 * [combine]
 * method=sigmaMean
 * sigmaThreshold=5
 * minGoodFract=0
 * noDerotate=false
 *
 * [output]
 * directory=./p4-output
 * fileName=finim_
 * exactFName=false
 * outputPSFSub=false
 * \endcode
 *
 * The comparison configuration does not promise bitwise-identical output. The prototype used float/CUDA PCA and
 * zero-filled unsupported pixels, whereas p4Reduce uses all-double CPU PCA and propagates authoritative validity
 * through derotation and combination. The prototype also wrote an unused `psf_mean.fits` sidecar that has no effect
 * on the reduction and is not reproduced by p4Reduce.
 *
 * For a new dataset, leave `preProcess.skip=false` and configure inherited preprocessing explicitly. Diagnostics do
 * not change the numerical result, but the ownership and region-summary products are useful when validating new
 * geometry. `p4Validity_*.fits` records detector-frame residual validity immediately after local fitting. Final
 * products record `HIERARCH P4 FRAME = 'detector'`.
 *
 * \section p4reduce_specialized_guides Specialized workflows
 *
 * Continue with these focused pages as needed:
 *
 * - \ref p4_local_user_guide "Pixel-Local Processing" for exact finite-amplitude bounded-stamp evaluation;
 * - \ref p4_optimizer_user_guide "Negative-Planet Optimization" for contrast and position fitting;
 * - \ref p4_psf_user_guide "Frozen-Model PSF Responses" for analytic response reconstruction and filtering; and
 * - \ref p4_rotated_user_guide "Rotated-Frame Regression (Negative Result)" for the unsuccessful experiment retained
 *   as a numerical reference.
 *
 * \section p4reduce_dictionary Configuration reference
 *
 * The \ref p4_configuration_dictionary "p4Reduce configuration dictionary" gives the command-line spelling,
 * configuration-file form, accepted values, and detailed scientific effect of every P4 setting. The shared
 * \ref common_configuration_dictionary "common dictionary" covers input, preprocessing, ADI, combination, and output.
 *
 * @}
 */
